{#
  domain-label.njk — single source of truth for emitting a domain's label.

  This is the ONLY place anywhere on the site that knows how to derive a
  human-facing label from a domain collection item. Every template that
  wants to display a domain's name imports this module and calls its macros.
  Never reach into domain.data.title or domain.data.shortTitle directly
  from elsewhere — go through these macros so any future change to the data
  shape (e.g., a move to _data/domains.json, a per-locale rename) lands in
  exactly one file.

  Usage:

    Import once at the top of a template:
      {%- import "partials/domain-label.njk" as domainLabel -%}

    Then call:
      {{ domainLabel.full(domain) }}      — canonical long title
      {{ domainLabel.short(domain) }}     — compact label; falls back to full

  Macros return strings, so they're safe inside attributes, e.g.:
    <a data-title="{{ domainLabel.full(domain) }}" href="...">

  Argument:
    domain — a collection item (e.g., from collections.domains).
             The macro reads domain.data.title and domain.data.shortTitle.
#}

{% macro full(domain) -%}
{{- domain.data.title -}}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro short(domain) -%}
{{- domain.data.shortTitle or domain.data.title -}}
{%- endmacro %}
